@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
-`/link` verifies the name exists via Mojang, then checks the live `/guild list` roster of **every connected
-guild** and accepts membership of any one of them. It **fails open only when the result is inconclusive** — no
-bot connected, a timeout, output that never looked like a roster — and never when a roster parsed cleanly and
-the name was absent. Across guilds that means: found if any roster has them, absent only if every roster
-parsed cleanly and none did, inconclusive otherwise. Note the check necessarily weakens as guilds are added,
-since one flaky roster makes the whole thing inconclusive.
+`/link` verifies the name exists via Mojang, then checks guild membership. With `HYPIXEL_API_KEY` set it asks
+the Hypixel public API first (`/v2/guild` for the player's UUID) and compares that guild against each bridged
+guild's stored Hypixel guild id (learned on bot spawn). If the API cannot decide — missing key, HTTP failure,
+or the registry has nothing to compare against yet — it falls back to the live `/guild list` roster of **every
+connected guild**, and accepts membership of any one of them. It **fails open only when the result is
+inconclusive** — no bot connected, a timeout, output that never looked like a roster, and no API answer —
+and never when a roster (or the API) showed the player was absent. Across guilds that means: found if any
+bridged guild has them, absent only when membership was checked cleanly and none did, inconclusive otherwise.
+Note the chat fallback necessarily weakens as guilds are added, since one flaky roster makes the whole chat
+check inconclusive.
